// TPM2_ObjectChangeAuth is used to change the authorization secret for a
// TPM-resident object.
//
// If successful, a new private area for the TPM-resident object associated with
// objectHandle is returned, which includes the new authorization value.
//
// This command does not change the authorization of the TPM-resident object on
// which it operates. Therefore, the old authValue (of the TPM-resident object)
// is used when generating the response HMAC key if required.
//
// This command may not be used to change the authorization value for an NV
// Index or a Primary Object.
TpmTestVector(
  name: "[TPM2_ObjectChangeAuth] bad object type",
  spec_versions: [
    184,
  ],
  test_sequence: [
  ]
)
